  "articleBody": "Ever wonder why a newly framed wall just doesn't look quite right? There are several common mistakes that can lead to less-than-perfect results in wall framing, and it's easy to fall into these traps if you're not careful. One of the biggest errors is using incorrect stud spacing. This can affect the stability of the wall and how well drywall or other finishes sit on it. Another frequent blunder is skipping the crucial step of layout checks. You might think you've measured everything perfectly, but a quick re-check before you start cutting and nailing can save a lot of headaches. It's also vital to fasten the bottom and top plates correctly; if they're not secure, the entire wall's stability is compromised. And here’s a big one: not keeping walls in plane or plumb. This means your wall could be leaning or bowed, making it a nightmare for finishing. You’ll also want to make sure you’re using the right fasteners and methods for connecting the new framing to any existing structures. For load-bearing walls or complex openings, these mistakes can become serious safety concerns. That's why, especially for anything structural or critical to your home's integrity, bringing in an experienced professional like HH Remodeling is your best bet to avoid these common pitfalls and ensure a solid, straight wall.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
